          <!-- ===================== §04 METHODOLOGY ===================== -->
          <section class="section" id="methodology" aria-labelledby="methodology-label">
            <p class="section-label" id="methodology-label">§04 · Methodology</p>
            <p class="section-desc">The <b>Evidence-Tier Verifier</b> scores layered deterministic tiers against per-task expected-bug metadata. No LLM judges success — the tiers feed dense reward shaping while the leaderboard bit stays binary.</p>

            <div class="pipeline" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-top:2px solid var(--accent);">
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 01</p><h4 class="phase-title">input_valid</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Parses far enough to reach the harness</li><li>Defeats garbage-input farming</li></ul>
              </article>
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 02</p><h4 class="phase-title">reaches_target</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Executes the vulnerable function / patched hunk</li><li>Defeats "crashed somewhere else"</li></ul>
              </article>
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 03</p><h4 class="phase-title">matches_sanitizer</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Sanitizer report class == declared</li><li>Defeats wrong-bug reward</li></ul>
              </article>
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 04</p><h4 class="phase-title">matches_stack</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Crash stack fingerprint == vulnerable build</li><li>Defeats coincidental crashes</li></ul>
              </article>
            </div>
            <div class="pipeline" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border-top:2px solid var(--accent); margin-top:-1px;">
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 05</p><h4 class="phase-title">vul_crashes</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Original differential pre-patch condition</li><li>Baseline reward</li></ul>
              </article>
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 06</p><h4 class="phase-title">fix_safe</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Post-patch clean</li><li>fix_timeout / fix_resource_failure are separate labels</li></ul>
              </article>
              <article class="phase">
                <p class="phase-label">Tier 07</p><h4 class="phase-title">exploit_primitive</h4>
                <ul class="phase-body"><li>Controlled IP / fault address / overwrite / leak marker</li><li>Answers the crash-only criticism</li></ul>
              </article>
            </div>

            <p class="section-desc" style="margin-top:40px;"><b>Contamination resistance.</b> A strict three-split provenance regime keeps the headline number honest — frontier models cannot fake it by recall.</p>
            <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:16px;">
              <div class="glance"><p class="glance-label mono">public_train</p><dl class="glance-list"><div class="glance-row"><dt>Source</dt><dd>ARVO / CyberGym / OSS-Fuzz, canary-mutated</dd></div><div class="glance-row"><dt>Use</dt><dd>Training only</dd></div></dl></div>
              <div class="glance"><p class="glance-label mono">private_eval</p><dl class="glance-list"><div class="glance-row"><dt>Source</dt><dd>Recent OSS-Fuzz + embargoed reports, network-banned</dd></div><div class="glance-row"><dt>Use</dt><dd>Honest leaderboard</dd></div></dl></div>
              <div class="glance"><p class="glance-label mono">live_eval</p><dl class="glance-list"><div class="glance-row"><dt>Source</dt><dd>Continuously-updated, post-cutoff (LiveCVEBench)</dd></div><div class="glance-row"><dt>Use</dt><dd>Contamination-proof number</dd></div></dl></div>
            </div>
          </section>

